<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teresa, Countess of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1080–1130</span> · Also known as Teresa of León</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teresa was a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> of León and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> who, with her husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-count-of-portugal">Henry of Burgundy</a>, held the County of Portugal from 1096. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s death in 1112 she ruled alone, styling herself queen, and allied with the Galician Trava family. Her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso Henriques</a> defeated her supporters at São Mamede in 1128 and drove her into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, where she died in 1130.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teresa-countess-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Teresa, Countess of Portugal" width="320" height="671" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theresa_of_Portugal_(1080-1130)_mini.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
